Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] Servers: avatar bakes held to 512 within the texture
 budget; IbashoAgent textureStats

On Second Life, a busy region passed IbashoTextureBudget four- to sixfold. Avatars there wear
2048x2048 bakes, and the viewer keeps them whole: bake textures are never scaled down, and the head,
upper and lower bakes carry a loaded callback at discard 0 (for the morph masks) that pins their
desired level at 0 whatever the discard bias says. In London City, 37 such bakes were 790 of the
viewer's 1,547 MB of textures, and my own avatar's bakes and wearables another 187.

While IbashoTextureBudget is set, avatar bakes and my own avatar's textures are now held to 512, and
the world's textures to RenderMaxTextureResolution, after the callbacks have had their say, on screen
or off. Textures above the limit are scaled down, bakes included, and so are fetched (not LOD)
textures such as my own avatar's wearables, which arrive whole before their size is known. Off
servers (no budget) nothing changes. A bake's morph-mask callback then never sees discard 0, which
only matters to system-body alpha masks.

IbashoAgent textureStats says where texture memory goes: totals, the discard bias, and the textures by
boost level and size, with the largest few.
